       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day, which is five times the maximum daily dose of oral ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day under prescription labeling, and usually 2,400 mg/day or less in practice). A single 4000 mg dose is also far above the usual 400\u2013800 mg maximum. A dose like this risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and metabolic toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo, for example 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg/day) or 800 mg three times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want. If you really do intend 4000 mg per dose, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it to the order note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
