       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 16,000 mg/day of ibuprofen has no recognized therapeutic use. It is well into the range where serious harm is expected, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. Entering it would put it in front of nursing staff as a valid order.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Corrected dose:** Give me the dose you intended, such as 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Different goal:** If you're trying to reach a specific effect, such as maximal anti-inflammatory dosing or stronger analgesia, I can enter an order within labeled limits. A pharmacist can also help with alternatives.\n- **Unusual indication:** If there's a protocol or clinical context I don't know about, please take it through pharmacy review or your institution's override process. I can't enter it as a standard order.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?"
